1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,980
Last time, the trolley was metal: strong.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:06,530
The fish tank was glass: transparent and waterproof.

3
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:08,610
Now: three water bottles!

4
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:12,400
Lock in first.

5
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:15,080
A little squirrel is hiding in this video.

6
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:16,570
Can you spot it?

7
00:00:17,149 --> 00:00:18,479
Today you'll learn:

8
00:00:18,676 --> 00:00:20,946
One object, different materials.

9
00:00:21,147 --> 00:00:23,247
Many materials, one object.

10
00:00:23,451 --> 00:00:25,481
Choosing a suitable material.

11
00:00:27,163 --> 00:00:28,043
Round one.

12
00:00:28,343 --> 00:00:29,933
A water bottle for school.

13
00:00:30,213 --> 00:00:32,793
It must not break when dropped, and you want to see the

14
00:00:32,813 --> 00:00:33,943
water inside.

15
00:00:34,223 --> 00:00:35,433
One, plastic.

16
00:00:35,703 --> 00:00:36,713
Two, glass.

17
00:00:36,993 --> 00:00:37,983
Three, metal.

18
00:00:38,263 --> 00:00:39,743
Show me with your fingers.

19
00:00:46,214 --> 00:00:47,194
Locked in!

20
00:00:47,322 --> 00:00:48,042
Three!

21
00:00:48,332 --> 00:00:49,632
Metal is strong!

22
00:00:49,681 --> 00:00:50,291
One!

23
00:00:50,441 --> 00:00:52,511
I drop mine every PE lesson.

24
00:00:52,581 --> 00:00:53,781
Not one crack!

25
00:00:53,830 --> 00:00:54,560
One.

26
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:56,768
Look closer.

27
00:00:57,388 --> 00:00:59,358
Three bottles, full of water.

28
00:00:59,668 --> 00:01:00,758
No drips.

29
00:01:01,318 --> 00:01:04,348
Plastic, glass and metal are all waterproof.

30
00:01:05,357 --> 00:01:06,747
Can we see the water?

31
00:01:07,347 --> 00:01:08,607
Plastic, yes.

32
00:01:09,187 --> 00:01:10,307
Glass, yes.

33
00:01:10,897 --> 00:01:11,977
Metal, no.

34
00:01:12,687 --> 00:01:13,867
Now, a drop.

35
00:01:14,447 --> 00:01:16,347
The plastic bottle bounces.

36
00:01:16,937 --> 00:01:17,987
No break!

37
00:01:18,497 --> 00:01:19,737
The glass bottle?

38
00:01:20,317 --> 00:01:21,927
We do not drop glass.

39
00:01:22,062 --> 00:01:24,762
Glass is not as strong as plastic or metal.

40
00:01:28,887 --> 00:01:30,187
The answer is one.

41
00:01:30,457 --> 00:01:31,377
Plastic!

42
00:01:31,667 --> 00:01:32,657
One finger?

43
00:01:32,977 --> 00:01:34,177
One finger up!

44
00:01:34,223 --> 00:01:34,813
Oh!

45
00:01:35,073 --> 00:01:37,233
Strong, but I cannot see my water!

46
00:01:37,661 --> 00:01:38,821
Say it with me!

47
00:01:39,527 --> 00:01:42,117
An object can be made from different materials.

48
00:01:42,687 --> 00:01:46,047
The choice of materials depends on the use of the object.

49
00:01:50,921 --> 00:01:52,191
Now look closer.

50
00:01:52,491 --> 00:01:53,611
A parked car.

51
00:01:54,266 --> 00:01:55,826
The tyres: rubber.

52
00:01:56,436 --> 00:01:57,946
They carry the whole car.

53
00:01:58,576 --> 00:01:59,846
Rubber is strong.

54
00:02:00,458 --> 00:02:02,088
The seats: fabric.

55
00:02:02,638 --> 00:02:04,068
Press, and they bend.

56
00:02:04,648 --> 00:02:06,208
Fabric is flexible.

57
00:02:06,821 --> 00:02:08,611
The windscreen: glass.

58
00:02:09,201 --> 00:02:12,671
Water cannot pass through, and we can see through it clearly.

59
00:02:13,296 --> 00:02:14,556
The body: metal.

60
00:02:14,576 --> 00:02:18,086
Strong, to protect the people inside.

61
00:02:19,492 --> 00:02:20,522
One car.

62
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:22,382
Four parts.

63
00:02:22,982 --> 00:02:24,212
Four materials!

64
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:28,822
Say it with me!

65
00:02:29,533 --> 00:02:33,123
The materials are selected for the different functions of the parts based

66
00:02:33,143 --> 00:02:34,793
on their physical properties.

67
00:02:37,269 --> 00:02:39,099
Each part has its own job.

68
00:02:39,389 --> 00:02:41,629
So each part gets its own material.

69
00:02:41,976 --> 00:02:43,306
Be a drop of water!

70
00:02:43,656 --> 00:02:44,636
Shrink down.

71
00:02:44,906 --> 00:02:45,836
Quietly.

72
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:51,496
You are a drop of water, falling from a watering can.

73
00:02:52,233 --> 00:02:53,183
Splash!

74
00:02:53,963 --> 00:02:55,453
You land on the glass.

75
00:02:56,233 --> 00:02:57,723
You cannot pass through.

76
00:02:58,388 --> 00:03:01,818
Through the glass, you see the fabric seats, dry inside.

77
00:03:02,555 --> 00:03:06,185
You roll over the metal, past the rubber tyre, to the ground.

78
00:03:08,589 --> 00:03:09,489
My notes!

79
00:03:09,619 --> 00:03:12,179
One: rubber tyres, because rubber is strong.

80
00:03:12,239 --> 00:03:15,809
Two: a glass windscreen, because glass is made from sand.

81
00:03:15,879 --> 00:03:18,829
Three: fabric seats, because fabric is flexible.

82
00:03:19,103 --> 00:03:20,003
Showdown!

83
00:03:20,313 --> 00:03:21,443
Double points.

84
00:03:21,713 --> 00:03:23,333
One line has a mistake.

85
00:03:23,623 --> 00:03:25,383
Line one, two, or three?

86
00:03:25,683 --> 00:03:27,153
Show me with your fingers.

87
00:03:33,628 --> 00:03:34,608
Locked in!

88
00:03:34,736 --> 00:03:35,366
Two!

89
00:03:35,516 --> 00:03:37,146
Sand is where glass comes from.

90
00:03:37,286 --> 00:03:38,676
It is not a property!

91
00:03:38,724 --> 00:03:39,514
Two.

92
00:03:39,764 --> 00:03:41,414
Glass is waterproof!

93
00:03:43,391 --> 00:03:44,431
Two fingers?

94
00:03:44,671 --> 00:03:46,601
Put up two more on your score hand!

95
00:03:46,799 --> 00:03:48,059
Name the property.

96
00:03:48,339 --> 00:03:49,909
Then link it to the job.

97
00:03:51,343 --> 00:03:55,993
It is important to choose a material whose physical property is suitable

98
00:03:56,173 --> 00:03:58,613
for the intended use of the object.

99
00:04:00,088 --> 00:04:01,193
Say it with us!

100
00:04:01,853 --> 00:04:03,008
What is it for?

101
00:04:03,433 --> 00:04:04,414
The purpose!

102
00:04:08,253 --> 00:04:09,405
What can it do?

103
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:10,915
The property!

104
00:04:14,653 --> 00:04:15,693
So choose!

105
00:04:16,233 --> 00:04:17,709
A suitable material!

106
00:04:21,808 --> 00:04:23,278
Show me your score hand!

107
00:04:23,558 --> 00:04:24,608
More than one?

108
00:04:24,908 --> 00:04:26,268
You beat the Buddies.

109
00:04:26,568 --> 00:04:27,628
Three fingers?

110
00:04:27,898 --> 00:04:28,908
High five!

111
00:04:29,263 --> 00:04:30,653
Did you spot the squirrel?

112
00:04:30,933 --> 00:04:32,793
It was on the tree by the cars!

113
00:04:32,988 --> 00:04:33,591
Fun fact!

114
00:04:33,611 --> 00:04:37,641
A squirrel's nest has strong twigs outside and soft leaves inside.

115
00:04:37,661 --> 00:04:40,193
Different materials for different jobs!

116
00:04:40,432 --> 00:04:41,712
Tell someone at home!

117
00:04:42,501 --> 00:04:44,361
Next time: a school bag!

118
00:04:44,641 --> 00:04:47,331
Its strap must bend, and it must not tear.

119
00:04:47,611 --> 00:04:49,411
Which material would you choose?

120
00:04:49,681 --> 00:04:50,761
One, fabric.

121
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:52,011
Two, metal.

122
00:04:52,281 --> 00:04:53,261
Three, wood.

123
00:04:53,541 --> 00:04:54,861
Lock in your answer!

124
00:04:54,909 --> 00:04:56,029
A metal strap!

125
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:57,539
Nothing can tear that!

126
00:04:58,265 --> 00:05:00,465
Let's read today's key words together!

127
00:05:00,755 --> 00:05:01,515
Ready?

128
00:05:01,802 --> 00:05:02,612
Use.

129
00:05:03,836 --> 00:05:04,636
Parts.

130
00:05:05,890 --> 00:05:06,740
Suitable.

131
00:05:08,091 --> 00:05:09,031
Well done!

132
00:05:10,013 --> 00:05:11,114
Say it with us!

133
00:05:11,915 --> 00:05:12,665
Ready?

134
00:05:12,788 --> 00:05:13,448
One!

135
00:05:13,788 --> 00:05:14,488
two!

136
00:05:14,793 --> 00:05:15,968
Now you know!
